o v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback the service reports healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52323, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01KFeSWqQBxdzqAhgUQ6nF5y", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52323, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KFeSWqQBxdzqAhgUQ6nF5y", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 56014, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n1. **Before the rollback:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0. A follow-up check shows the service healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n3. **Incident:** The first request to open the incident timed out. I confirmed nothing had been created, then retried using the same idempotency key so it couldn't create a duplicate. INC-0001 is open and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the failure, the rollback and the result, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure should be found before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Do4BJFMqH3Mwn5DKQHBCvU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RVYriCqqhwzqrdcvCaq