me": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "No incident was recorded, so I'm retrying with the same idempotency key to avoid creating a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KFeSWqQBxdzqAhgUQ6nF5y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. Rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback the service reports healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n1. **Before the rollback:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0. A follow-up check shows the service healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n3. **Incident:** The first request to open the incident timed out. I confirmed nothing had been created, then retried using the same idempotency key so it couldn't create a duplicate. INC-0001 is open and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the failure, the rollback and the result, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure should be found before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}